cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use base16384-js, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "base16384-js: an encoder and decoder for the base16384 text format in JavaScript"
abstract: >-
  An independent, dependency-free JavaScript implementation of the base16384
  binary-to-text format, which writes 14 bits per character using the code
  points U+4E00 to U+8DFF. Compatible with the reference command-line tool in
  both directions, with strict validation, streaming and a command-line tool.
authors:
  - name: "Aesthetic Vulpes"
    website: "https://github.com/didvc/"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-01
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/DecodeEncode/base16384-js"
url: "https://decodeencode.github.io/base16384-js/"
keywords:
  - base16384
  - binary-to-text encoding
  - UTF-16
  - streaming
